      "writtenOn": "2023-02-07T14:07:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "WIFI NAN hash is 64bit long value \"uint64_t inHash\" , NAN application generate hash code using some hash api as long value \u0026 finally It gets converted to byte array by NAN APP. \nBy default Byte buffer(ByteBuffer buffer \u003d ByteBuffer.allocate(Long.BYTES);buffer.putLong(x);) keeps data in BIG endian format(eg. aa, bb, .., hh), But controller generally expects  Little endian format(eg. hh,.. aa) for uint64_t  hash.\n\nI think, if we need to remove this code from stack, we can  add comment in SDK API eg, WIFI NAN HASH byte array data must be little endian  format? So application must pass WIFI NAN HASH byte array in little endian, what is your view on this?",
